+def _ours_board_changes(grid_a: Any, grid_b: Any, border: int) -> list[str] | None:
+    """Exact object changes between two boards as prompt lines (None when their shapes differ).
+
+    Objects are his segments (4-connected, one colour). An object whose box lies inside the outer `border` cells
+    (HUD and budget bars) is not compared. Every line is a plain statement about the two boards:
+    - moved / rotated: the only object of that shape and colour on each board is at a new place / pose;
+    - recolored: the same shape at the same place has another colour;
+    - disappeared / appeared: objects of a shape and colour at places where the other board has none of them
+      (several alike objects are listed by place, never paired into moves).
+    Not listed (the caller's wording says "include"): parts carried along by a moved object, cells a moved object
+    now covers or has uncovered, and same-colour regions that only changed shape around the changes.
+    """
